/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Current is a stream of separate electrons.
   - ish² = 2q(Ip + Id)B
   - ish² is the mean-square shot-noise current in A²; q = 1.602 × 10⁻¹⁹ C; Ip is the photocurrent and Id the dark current, both in A; B is in Hz.
   - Dark current is the current that flows with no light: carriers made by heat in the depleted volume (the bulk part, Idb) plus leakage along the surface of the chip (Ids).
   - ish² = 2q(Ip + Idb)M²FB + 2qIdsB
   - M is the avalanche gain and F the excess noise factor.
   - Thermal (Johnson) noise is the random motion of electrons in the load resistor RL.
   - ith² = 4kBTB/RL
   - kB = 1.38 × 10⁻²³ J/K is Boltzmann's constant, T the temperature in K and RL the load resistance in Ω.
   - The noise sources are independent, so their mean squares (powers) add: σ² = ish² + ith², where σ is the total rms noise current.
*/
