/* book exam traps: Adding rms noise currents. Add the mean squares, then take one square root. | Leaving the dark current out of the shot-noise term. | In an APD, multiplying all of the dark current by M²F. Only the bulk part is multiplied; surface leakage adds 2qIdsB unmultiplied. | Treating a bigger RL as free. It lowers thermal noise but raises RLC and narrows the bandwidth. | Quoting SNR(dB) as 20 log₁₀ of the power ratio. SNR here is already a ratio of mean squares (powers), so use 10 log₁₀. */
